<div class="note"><b class="h">Local claim risks</b><ul class="chips"><li>Hail</li><li>Wind</li><li>Fox River flooding</li><li>Ice dams</li><li>Tornadoes</li></ul><p class="housing"><b>Housing mix:</b> Victorian homes in the historic districts, post-war bungalows and ranches, west-side subdivisions.</p></div>

<h2>Elgin’s historic housing</h2>
<p>Elgin grew as a manufacturing town along the Fox River, and its historic districts — including Gifford Park and the Elgin Historic District near downtown — are lined with Victorian, Queen Anne and Italianate homes. Many have wood clapboard siding, slate or multi-layer roofs, ornate trim and plaster walls. West of Randall Road, newer subdivisions add a very different kind of claim.</p>
<h2>Storms along the Fox</h2>
<p>Elgin’s history includes the 1920 Palm Sunday tornado that struck downtown. Today, hail and severe thunderstorms are more common, along with Fox River flooding in wet springs and ice dams on steep older roofs every winter.</p>
<h2>Common Elgin disputes</h2>
<ul>
<li>Victorian homes where trim, siding and slate are priced with modern substitutes.</li>
<li>Ice dam damage to plaster ceilings and walls.</li>
<li>Newer homes with partial siding approvals and discontinued profiles.</li>
<li>Flood versus covered water questions near the river.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Serving Elgin and nearby towns</h2>
<p>We serve Elgin, South Elgin, Bartlett, Carpentersville, St. Charles and Hampshire.</p>

<h2>Services available in Elgin</h2>
<p>Every Illinois Insurance Appraiser service is available to property owners in Elgin and nearby communities, including:</p>
