<h2>Questions from Elgin owners</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>My older home has original wood siding. Can it be matched?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="a"><p>Sometimes, with custom milling. If matching isn’t possible, the repair may need to extend further. We document profile, exposure and availability.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does the city’s historic commission affect insurance repairs?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="a"><p>For homes in designated districts, exterior changes may need approval. Those requirements can affect materials and cost.</p></div></details></div>
